"""Odds-free LightGBM win model trained directly on the per-race softmax likelihood,
plus a market-aware stage-2 blend with honest out-of-month validation.

Changes vs. the binary-classifier version

-----------------------------------------
1. Listwise objective. Trees add to a per-runner utility u_j and the loss is the same
   race-softmax cross-entropy the conditional logit optimises:
       L_r = -sum_j y_j * log softmax_r(u)_j      (dead heat: y_j = 1/k on each winner)
       g_j = p_j - y_j,   h_j = 2 p_j (1 - p_j)   (XGBoost-style diagonal bound)
   Binary logloss + post-hoc renormalisation optimises a different quantity and weights
   races by field size. Early stopping uses the metric you report (per-race log loss).
2. Context features: within-race rank percentiles of the key form/connection rates and
   field size, which trees cannot derive from per-runner columns. Monotone constraints
   on the features whose sign is not in doubt (regularises the Kaggle -> HKJC shift).
3. Seed bagging: average raw utilities over several subsample seeds.
4. Stage 2: ridge-to-market blend, theta ~ (1, 0, 0), penalty chosen by leave-one-month-out
   CV inside h_s2 (never touching h_test). Reports mkt+lgbm, mkt+cl and mkt+lgbm+cl so the
   marginal contribution of each stage-1 model is visible.
Requires lightgbm >= 4.0 (callable objective in params).
"""

